  "term": "Laurence–Moon–Bardet–Biedl syndrome",
  "definition": "Laurence–Moon–Bardet–Biedl syndrome is an inherited autosomal recessive condition marked by retinitis pigmentosa, extra fingers or toes, obesity, cognitive impairment, underdeveloped genitals, kidney malformation, and short stature. In the source packet, it is described as distinct from Laurence-Moon syndrome.",
